                            CONTRIBUTING
Email only. No pull requests or GitHub Issues. Changes require an RFC
(request for comments) before a patch series. Send your proposal to
the engineering team at contact@podomy.com.

This includes new subsystems, protocol changes, and architectural
decisions. Patch series sent without prior email discussion will be redirected
there before code review.

Do not use GitHub Issues or pull requests. Report bugs and propose work by
email to contact@podomy.com.

                         Review Expectations

Small patch (bugfix)    3 business days
Normal patch            7 days
RFC                     7 days

If maintainers cannot meet the window, they will say so. Silence is
not a no.

                          Getting Started
Prerequisites  Go >=1.26.3 and golangci-lint v2.14.0
+               Install: https://golangci-lint.run/welcome/install/

1. Build        go build ./cmd/concord
2. Verify       go run ./check/   # tidy + golangci-lint fmt (gofumpt/goimports @.golangci.yml:7) + goheader fix + golangci-lint run + go test + git diff --exit-code
3. Test         go test ./...   # already in verify
4. Pick an area in the code or a bug reported by email

Local check, not a step: git config core.hooksPath .githooks runs the
verify script on every commit via .githooks/pre-commit. It never leaves the
machine; a commit is done when the hook passes.

5. Send an RFC to contact@podomy.com if the change is not small
6. Export with git format-patch and send with git send-email to contact@podomy.com.
   Your Author name and email stay on the commit; a maintainer applies it and
   appears as committer. Submission accepts the CLA and follows /COMMITS.
